{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "GROUNDING: The printed output does not contain the claimed numbers (Number of patients after filtering and deduplication: 712, Mean biomarker_final: 134.72). The only shown output is a series of patient_id counts, so the quantitative claims are unsupported.",
    "SCOPE: The contract asks for the mean across all patients. The analyst excluded any patient with biomarker_baseline == -999, even if that patient has a valid biomarker_final value. This removes patients from the defined population without justification in the contract.",
    "UNACKNOWLEDGED DATA PROBLEMS: The analyst assumes that rows with biomarker_baseline == -999 should be dropped, but the sentinel indicates a missing baseline, not necessarily a missing final measurement. This potential bias is not discussed."
  ]
}
